<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Cyrene</h1><p class="st-meta">440 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.) · capital Cyrene</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cyrene after its kings, a quarrelsome Greek republic famous for silphium, horses and the Cyrenaic school of philosophy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 440 BCE the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battiad-dynasty">Battiad</a> king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-iv">Arcesilaus IV</a>, was overthrown and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyrene">Kingdom of Cyrene</a> became a republic. The city remained the leading power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>, a group of Greek cities later called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pentapolis-cyrenaica">Pentapolis</a>, together with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barca">Barca</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/euesperides">Euesperides</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taucheira">Taucheira</a> and its own port, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollonia-cyrenaica">Apollonia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Government swung between democracy and oligarchy, with bloody civil strife in the early 4th century BCE. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> remained rich from silphium, grain and horses, and it treated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> over its western border at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altars-of-the-philaeni">Altars of the Philaeni</a>. It was an intellectual centre: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristippus-of-cyrene">Aristippus</a> founded the Cyrenaic school of philosophy, and the mathematician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodorus-of-cyrene">Theodorus</a> taught there. Cyrene submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in 331 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 324 to 322 BCE the Spartan adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thibron">Thibron</a> attacked the city, and its factions called in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a>, whose general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ophellas">Ophellas</a> annexed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a> in 322 BCE. It later became the centre of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ptolemaic-kingdom-of-cyrene">Ptolemaic Kingdom of Cyrene</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 440 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:50.95%;width:2.35%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>440 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cyrene</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cyrene</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-381&amp;focus=republic-of-cyrene" aria-label="Republic of Cyrene on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5240 985 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Cyrene lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5560 1241L5560 1241M5560 1241L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5560 1241h0M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5560 1241h0"/><path class="ma